<newsitem itemid="184083" id="root" date="1996-11-12" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: General Accident 9-month profits down.</title>
<headline>General Accident 9-month profits down.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months ended September 30</p>
<p>				   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		72.0		   vs 64.2</p>
<p> Pretax oper profit    311.0		   vs 351.0</p>
<p> Pretax		    511.0		   vs 436.0</p>
<p> Total premium income  4.787 bln	     vs 4.433 bln</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts forecasts on UK composite insurer General Accident's nine months pretax operating profits were in a range of 300 to 324 million stg.</p>
<p> Long term income	 1.34 bln	     vs 1.131 bln</p>
<p> General income	   3.447 bln	    vs 3.302 bln</p>
<p> *Underwriting result    166.0 loss	   vs 62.0 loss</p>
<p> Investment income	409.0		  vs 372.0</p>
<p> Investment gains	 200.0		  vs 85.0</p>
<p> Tax			  145.0		  vs 125.0</p>
<p> Attributable	     346.0		  vs 292.0</p>
<p>*NOTE - Worldwide underwriting deficit of 166 million includes increased severe weather losses of 58 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
